Package: RegCompassR
Title: Multiome Regulatory Evidence and Metabolic Reaction Analysis
Version: 1.8.9
Authors@R: c(person(given = "RegCompass", family = "Developers", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "dev@example.com"))
Author: RegCompass Developers [aut, cre]
Maintainer: RegCompass Developers <dev@example.com>
Description: Builds one validated Pando structural TF-peak-target candidate
    universe per cell type and jointly estimates a shared regulatory backbone
    plus condition-specific deviations for Human-GEM or Mouse-GEM GPR target
    genes in paired single-cell RNA and ATAC data. Full-size condition-stratified
    nonparametric bootstrap fits identify stable condition sub-GRNs, which define
    condition-specific metabolic target genes and complete-GPR core reactions.
    Biological meta-modules are deduplicated into one merged reaction catalogue
    without local FASTCORE completion. For each medium scenario, the package
    constructs one shared union GEM and performs one global FASTCORE completion
    before directional COMPASS-like scoring. Integrated RNA and ATAC evidence is
    converted to reaction penalties while preserving the same stoichiometric
    model across conditions. The canonical workflow is condition based and uses
    the current SuperCell2 strata-plus-label contract without a sample-column
    argument. Final results retain primary analysis tables and stage references,
    while detailed intermediate objects remain in their stage checkpoints.
